      "text": "300.\n</answer><|User|>The answer is correct. Can you also explain how to solve it using the distributive property of multiplication over addition?\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n<think>.\nCertainly! The distributive property of multiplication over addition states that for any three numbers a, b, and c, the equation a \u00d7 (b + c) = (a \u00d7 b) + (a \u00d7 c) holds true. We can use this property to break down the multiplication of 20 and 15 into simpler parts.\n</think>.\n<answer>. To use the distributive property, we can express 15 as the sum of 10 and 5. So, we have:\n20 \u00d7 15 = 20 \u00d7 (10 + 5)\nNow, we can apply the distributive property:\n20 \u00d7 (10 + 5) = (20 \u00d7 10) + (20 \u00d7 5)\nNext, we perform the multiplications:\n20 \u00d7 10 = 200\n20 \u00d7 5 = 100\nAdding these results together:\n200 + 100 = 300\nThus, the product of 20 and 15 is 300.\n</answer>",
