numbers \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), the equation \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\) holds true. We can use this property to simplify the multiplication of 64 and 17.\n\nHere's how we can apply the distributive property:\n\n1. **Rewrite 17 as \\(10 + 7\\):**\n   - \\(17 = 10 + 7\\).\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   - \\(64 \\times 17 = 64 \\times (10 + 7)\\).\n   - Using the distributive property, this becomes:\n     \\[\n     64 \\times 17 = 64 \\times 10 + 64 \\times 7\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - \\(64 \\times 10 = 640\\).\n   - \\(64 \\times 7 = 448\\).\n\n4. **Add the results:**\n   - \\(640 + 448 = 1088\\).\n\nSo, using the distributive property, we get:\n\\[\n64 \\times 17 = 640 + 448 = 1088\n\\]\n\nThis confirms that the product of 64 and 17 is indeed 1088.\n..\n</think>.\n<answer>\nUsing the distributive property, we can break down the multiplication as follows:\n\\[\n64 \\times 17 = 64 \\times (10 + 7) = 64 \\times 10 + 64 \\times 7\n\\]\nCalculating each part:\n\\[\n64 \\times 10 = 640\n\\]\n\\[\n64 \\times 7 = 448\n\\]\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n640 + 448 = 1088\n\\]\nTherefore, the product of 64 and 17 is 1088.\n</answer>",
